{"results":[{"url":"https://derrick-app.com/company/netflix/executives","final_url":"https://derrick-app.com/company/netflix/executives","title":"Netflix Leadership Team: 30 Executives (2026)","description":"Netflix's executive team includes 30 tracked leaders as of August 2026, led by Ted Sarandos (Co-Chief Executive Officer). The org chart, per-leader profiles and full leadership list are below.","language":"en","text":"Netflix's executive team includes 30 tracked leaders as of August 2026, led by Ted Sarandos (Co-Chief Executive Officer). The org chart, per-leader profiles and full leadership list are below.\n\n## Netflix executive team overview\n\nNetflix has 30 tracked executives leading key functions including company strategy and operations, financial strategy, technology strategy and engineering, marketing (as of August 2026). Netflix is one of the world's leading entertainment services, offering TV series, films, games and live programming across a wide variety of genres and languages. Members can play, pause and resume watching as much as they want, anytime and anywhere, and can change their plans at any time.\n\n## Netflix executive team org chart\n\nTSTed SarandosCo-Chief Executive Officer\n\n* GPGreg PetersCo-CEO\n* SNSpencer NeumannChief Financial Officer\n* ESElizabeth StoneChief Product and Technology Officer\n* MLMarian LeeChief Marketing Officer\n* BBBela BajariaChief Content Officer\n* DHDavid HymanChief Legal Officer\n* DDDani DudeckChief Communications Officer\n* SESergio EzamaChief Talent Officer\n* CWClete WillemsChief Global Affairs Officer\n* ARAmy ReinhardPresident of Advertising\n* ATAlain TascanPresident, Games\n* DLDan LinChairman of Netflix Film\n* MFMaria FerrerasGlobal Head of Partnerships\n* GHGagan HasteerVice President, Infrastructure Engineering\n* SWSpencer WangVice President, Finance, Investor Relations and Corporate Development\n* KNKate NortonVice President, Business Finance and Strategy\n* PPPablo Perez De RossoChief Financial Officer, EMEA\n* NGNatalie GutteridgeVice President, Corporate Legal and Operations\n* MHMagno HerranVice President, Global Brand and Partnership Marketing\n* JSJune SauvagetVice President, Marketing for EMEA and Asia-Pacific\n* JHJinny HoweHead of Scripted Series, US and Canada\n* BRBrandon RieggVice President, Nonfiction Series and Sports\n* MKMinyoung KimVice President, Content for Asia\n* LTLarry TanzVice President, Content for Europe, Middle East and Africa\n* FRFrancisco RamosVice President, Latin American Content\n* MSMonika ShergillVice President, Content, Netflix India\n* LSLauren SmithVice President, Content Programming Strategy and Operations and Global Licensing\n* WDWade DavisVice President, Inclusion Strategy\n* VTValarie TodaVice President, Talent\n\nGet this data with Derrick Find a company's people\n\n## Employees by management level\n\nProfiles by management levelEstimated\n\nProfiles by management level\n\n| Name | Profiles | Share |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| C-level | 30 | 0.2% |\n| VP | 260 | 1.4% |\n| Director | 900 | 4.8% |\n| Manager | 2,600 | 14% |\n| Individual contributor | 14,887 | 80% |\n\nGet this data with Derrick Find a company's people\n\n## Leadership team\n\n| Leader | Location | Email | Profile |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| TSTed SarandosCo-Chief Executive Officer |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n| GPGreg PetersCo-CEO |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n| SNSpencer NeumannChief Financial Officer |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n| ESElizabeth StoneChief Product and Technology Officer |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n| MLMarian LeeChief Marketing Officer |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n| BBBela BajariaChief Content Officer |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n| DHDavid HymanChief Legal Officer |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n| DDDani DudeckChief Communications Officer |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n| SESergio EzamaChief Talent Officer |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n| CWClete WillemsChief Global Affairs Officer |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n| ARAmy ReinhardPresident of Advertising |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n| ATAlain TascanPresident, Games |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n| DLDan LinChairman of Netflix Film |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n| MFMaria FerrerasGlobal Head of Partnerships |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n| GHGagan HasteerVice President, Infrastructure Engineering |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n| SWSpencer WangVice President, Finance, Investor Relations and Corporate Development |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n| KNKate NortonVice President, Business Finance and Strategy |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n| PPPablo Perez De RossoChief Financial Officer, EMEA |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n| NGNatalie GutteridgeVice President, Corporate Legal and Operations |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n| MHMagno HerranVice President, Global Brand and Partnership Marketing |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n| JSJune SauvagetVice President, Marketing for EMEA and Asia-Pacific |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n| JHJinny HoweHead of Scripted Series, US and Canada |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n| BRBrandon RieggVice President, Nonfiction Series and Sports |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n| MKMinyoung KimVice President, Content for Asia |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n| LTLarry TanzVice President, Content for Europe, Middle East and Africa |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n| FRFrancisco RamosVice President, Latin American Content |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n| MSMonika ShergillVice President, Content, Netflix India |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n| LSLauren SmithVice President, Content Programming Strategy and Operations and Global Licensing |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n| WDWade DavisVice President, Inclusion Strategy |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n| VTValarie TodaVice President, Talent |  | ••••@netflix.com | Profile → |\n\nGet this data with Derrick Find a company's people\n\nFind verified emails for the 30 leaders listed here and anyone else at Netflix in the Derrick web app (5 credits per email found), or track Netflix with Signal to be alerted when its leaders change jobs, it raises funds or starts hiring (Standard plan and up).\n\n## Netflix executive team roles\n\n### Ted Sarandos · full profile →\n\nCo-Chief Executive Officer\n\nTed Sarandos is Co-Chief Executive Officer of Netflix, a role he has held since 2020. He joined Netflix in 2000 and spent two decades building its content business, first as Chief Content Officer, shaping the company's move into original series and films. He oversees content, marketing, communications, legal and public policy.\n\n### Greg Peters · full profile →\n\nCo-CEO\n\nGreg Peters is Co-Chief Executive Officer of Netflix, appointed in 2023 after serving as Chief Operating Officer and Chief Product Officer. He joined Netflix in 2008 and led the company's international expansion, partnerships and product organization. He oversees product, technology, advertising, games and business operations.\n\n### Spencer Neumann · full profile →\n\nChief Financial Officer\n\nSpencer Neumann has been Netflix's Chief Financial Officer since January 2019. He joined from Activision Blizzard, where he was CFO, and before that spent much of his career at The Walt Disney Company, serving as CFO and Executive Vice President of Global Guest Experience for Disney Parks and Resorts. He also worked at the investment firms Providence Equity Partners and Summit Partners. He holds a bachelor's degree in economics and an MBA from Harvard, and sits on the board of Adobe.\n\n### Elizabeth Stone · full profile →\n\nChief Product and Technology Officer\n\nElizabeth Stone became Netflix's Chief Product and Technology Officer in February 2026, after serving as Chief Technology Officer from October 2023. She joined Netflix in 2020 to lead the data and insights organization. Before Netflix she was Chief Operating Officer at the healthcare technology company Nuna and Vice President of Science at Lyft, and earlier worked as a trader at Merrill Lynch and as an economist at Analysis Group. She studied at MIT and Stanford.\n\n### Marian Lee · full profile →\n\nChief Marketing Officer\n\nMarian Lee has been Netflix's Chief Marketing Officer since March 2022. She joined Netflix in 2021 as Vice President of Marketing for the US and Canada, arriving from Spotify, where she spent eight years in roles including Vice President and Co-Head of Music and Global Head of Artist and Label Services. Earlier in her career she worked at Conde Nast and J.Crew, and began at PwC in retail and consumer products consulting. She holds a B.A. from Barnard College.\n\n### Bela Bajaria · full profile →\n\nChief Content Officer\n\nBela Bajaria is Netflix's Chief Content Officer, a role she took in 2023, overseeing film, series and live programming across every country Netflix operates in, including Stranger Things, Squid Game and Bridgerton. She joined Netflix in 2016 and previously ran Universal Television as its President, after senior roles at CBS. She has been named to TIME's 100 Most Influential People and Fortune's Most Powerful Women, and serves on the board of The Coca-Cola Company.\n\n### David Hyman · full profile →\n\nChief Legal Officer\n\nDavid Hyman has been Netflix's Chief Legal Officer since 2002 and also serves as company Secretary, covering all legal and public policy matters. He is one of the longest-serving members of the leadership team, having joined before Netflix's 2002 IPO. He previously was General Counsel at the online grocery company Webvan, and practiced at the law firms Morrison and Foerster in San Francisco and Arent Fox in Washington DC. He holds a B.A. and a J.D. from the University of Virginia.\n\n### Dani Dudeck · full profile →\n\nChief Communications Officer\n\nDani Dudeck was named Netflix's Chief Communications Officer in December 2025. She spent roughly seven years as Chief Corporate Affairs Officer at Instacart, and before that was Chief Communications Officer at the game company Zynga and Vice President of Global Communications at MySpace. She earned bachelor's degrees in public relations and French from USC and serves on the board of USC Annenberg's Center for Public Relations.\n\n### Sergio Ezama · full profile →\n\nChief Talent Officer\n\nSergio Ezama has been Netflix's Chief Talent Officer since September 2021. He spent two decades at PepsiCo, which he joined in 2001, ending as Global Chief Talent Officer and Chief Human Resources Officer for global functions and groups, with postings across North America, Europe, Sub-Saharan Africa and Latin America. He holds a law degree and master's degrees from the University of Deusto in Spain, and completed Harvard Business School's General Management Program.\n\n### Clete Willems · full profile →\n\nChief Global Affairs Officer\n\nClete Willems joined Netflix as Chief Global Affairs Officer in April 2025. He was previously a partner at the law firm Akin Gump Strauss Hauer & Feld. During the first Trump administration he served as Deputy Assistant to the President for International Economics and Deputy Director of the National Economic Council, after working as a career attorney at the Office of the US Trade Representative throughout the Obama administration. He is a graduate of the University of Notre Dame and Georgetown University Law Center.\n\n### Amy Reinhard · full profile →\n\nPresident of Advertising\n\nAmy Reinhard is President of Advertising at Netflix, leading global ad sales, product, operations and measurement. She joined Netflix in 2016 as Vice President of Content Acquisition, later took on Consumer Products, and then ran Studio Operations, where she led the acquisitions of Scanline VFX and Animal Logic and the Fort Monmouth studio project. Before Netflix she was President of Worldwide TV Licensing and Distribution at Paramount Pictures. She holds a B.A. and an MBA from Harvard.\n\n### Alain Tascan · full profile →\n\nPresident, Games\n\nAlain Tascan has been President of Games at Netflix since July 2024. He arrived from Epic Games, where he was Executive Vice President of Game Development and oversaw first-party development on Fortnite, LEGO Fortnite, Rocket League and Fall Guys. Earlier he set up the Montreal studios for both Ubisoft and EA, with credits including Army of Two, Need for Speed: Nitro and Batman Vengeance, and founded the mobile studio Umi Games. He holds a master's degree in economics from the University of Nice.\n\n### Dan Lin · full profile →\n\nChairman of Netflix Film\n\nDan Lin became Chairman of Netflix Film in April 2024, taking over the company's film slate. He founded and ran the production company Rideback, where he produced the LEGO Movie franchise, Stephen King's It and the Sherlock Holmes films. Earlier he was Senior Vice President of Production at Warner Bros. Pictures, where his projects included Martin Scorsese's The Departed. He holds a B.S. in finance and marketing from the University of Pennsylvania and an MBA from Harvard.\n\n### Maria Ferreras · full profile →\n\nGlobal Head of Partnerships\n\nMaria Ferreras was named Global Head of Partnerships at Netflix in February 2021 and oversees the company's partnerships worldwide. She joined Netflix in 2017 as Vice President, Business Development for Europe, the Middle East and Africa. Before Netflix she spent 10 years at Google as Director of Partnerships for YouTube in Southern Europe and emerging markets, after senior roles at Lycos, Orange and Telecom Italia.\n\n### Gagan Hasteer · full profile →\n\nVice President, Infrastructure Engineering\n\nGagan Hasteer was named VP of Infrastructure Engineering at Netflix in February 2024, after serving as VP of Content Engineering and VP of Platform Engineering. He joined Netflix in 2011 and worked on initiatives including the launch of ads technology and live streaming. Before Netflix he co-founded Calypto, now part of Siemens, and led its engineering.\n\n### Spencer Wang · full profile →\n\nVice President, Finance, Investor Relations and Corporate Development\n\nSpencer Wang is Vice President of Finance, Investor Relations and Corporate Development at Netflix, where his remit includes the global P&L and M&A activity. He joined Netflix in March 2015 as VP of Finance and Investor Relations. Before Netflix he spent 16 years on Wall Street as an equity research analyst covering the Internet and Media sectors, including as Managing Director and Head of Media and Internet Equity Research at Credit Suisse First Boston.\n\n### Kate Norton · full profile →\n\nVice President, Business Finance and Strategy\n\nKate Norton was named VP of Business Finance & Strategy at Netflix in September 2025, after joining in 2024 as VP of Product & Commerce Finance & Strategy. Before Netflix she was a Managing Director and Partner at Boston Consulting Group, advising media, entertainment and technology companies in Europe and the US, and she later ran business operations at Workday.\n\n### Pablo Perez De Rosso · full profile →\n\nChief Financial Officer, EMEA\n\nPablo Perez De Rosso is Netflix's Chief Financial Officer for Europe, the Middle East and Africa. He previously led Strategy, FP&A, Production Finance and Customer Service globally. He joined Netflix in 2012 as one of the first executives dedicated to its Latin American business. Before Netflix he was Director of Business Development & Strategy at Universal Pictures and held roles at MGM Studios, Cinepolis and Lazard.\n\n### Natalie Gutteridge · full profile →\n\nVice President, Corporate Legal and Operations\n\nNatalie Gutteridge was named VP of Corporate Legal & Operations at Netflix in August 2024. She joined Netflix in 2016 in business affairs for local originals and content production across Europe, the Middle East, Africa and Latin America, and helped build the company's offices in Sao Paulo, Madrid and Mexico City. Before Netflix she worked at the BBC and TBWA/MAL.\n\n### Magno Herran · full profile →\n\nVice President, Global Brand and Partnership Marketing\n\nMagno Herran is VP of Global Brand and Partnership Marketing at Netflix, which he joined in 2016. He leads the global teams responsible for brand marketing and partnerships across Netflix's international business, including advertising and integrations. Before Netflix he held senior roles at Google, leading global brand, creative marketing and partnerships for mobile devices. He serves on the Effie Awards board.\n\n### June Sauvaget · full profile →\n\nVice President, Marketing for EMEA and Asia-Pacific\n\nJune Sauvaget was named VP of Marketing for Europe, the Middle East, Africa and Asia-Pacific at Netflix in January 2026, after joining in 2024 to lead marketing for Europe, the Middle East and Africa. Her marketing career has focused on launching and growing global brands in music, fashion, retail and beauty across Latin America, Asia, the Middle East, North America and Europe. Before Netflix she held roles at Spotify, Gap, Brex and Shiseido.\n\n### Jinny Howe · full profile →\n\nHead of Scripted Series, US and Canada\n\nJinny Howe became Netflix's Head of Scripted Series for the US and Canada in August 2025, when Peter Friedlander stepped down. She joined Netflix in 2018 to run drama series, after 13 years at John Wells Productions, where she became executive vice president of television and worked on Shameless, Southland and Animal Kingdom. At Netflix she has worked on series including Bridgerton, The Night Agent and The Diplomat.\n\n### Brandon Riegg · full profile →\n\nVice President, Nonfiction Series and Sports\n\nBrandon Riegg joined Netflix in November 2016 to build its first original unscripted slate and was promoted to vice president in March 2019. Before Netflix he was senior vice president and co-head of alternative programming at NBC, where he worked on The Voice and America's Got Talent. His teams oversee series such as Love Is Blind, Queer Eye and Formula 1: Drive to Survive, plus live sports events.\n\n### Minyoung Kim · full profile →\n\nVice President, Content for Asia\n\nMinyoung Kim has led Netflix's content for Asia, excluding India, since June 2021. She joined Netflix in 2016 as one of its first content executives in Asia Pacific, where she developed Korean original series and set up the Korea office. Before Netflix she led content partnerships at Twitter in Asia Pacific and also worked at NBCUniversal in France and CJ E&M in Korea. Her teams have overseen titles such as Squid Game and Alice in Borderland.\n\n### Larry Tanz · full profile →\n\nVice President, Content for Europe, Middle East and Africa\n\nLarry Tanz leads Netflix's content for Europe, the Middle East and Africa. He joined Netflix in 2014 and has worked on commissions, co-productions and acquisitions across several regions. Before Netflix he was CEO and president of Vuguru and of LivePlanet. He holds an MBA from Wharton and a BA in psychology from Harvard.\n\n### Francisco Ramos · full profile →\n\nVice President, Latin American Content\n\nFrancisco Ramos has led Latin American content at Netflix since October 2018, covering original series, films and licensed content for the region. Before Netflix he was an independent producer and worked at Antena 3 Television in Spain on acquisitions, production and programming. He began his career in Spain, including at the media group Grupo Zeta.\n\n### Monika Shergill · full profile →\n\nVice President, Content, Netflix India\n\nMonika Shergill has led content at Netflix India since July 2019. She joined from Viacom18, where she was executive vice president and head of content for Viacom18 Digital Ventures and helped launch its streaming service Voot. Earlier she held programming roles at Star India, and she began her career as a journalist and documentary filmmaker. At Netflix India she has overseen series and films such as Delhi Crime, Kohrra and Kaala Paani.\n\n### Lauren Smith · full profile →\n\nVice President, Content Programming Strategy and Operations and Global Licensing\n\nLauren Smith has led content programming strategy, operations and global licensing at Netflix since June 2024. Before that she led finance and strategy for content, studio and marketing. She joined Netflix in 2011, during the DVD era and the start of its international expansion, and worked on the deal with The CW, the series You and Lucifer, the global partnership with WWE and the film deals with NBCUniversal and Sony.\n\n### Wade Davis · full profile →\n\nVice President, Inclusion Strategy\n\nWade Davis was promoted to lead Netflix's inclusion team in 2023, when Verna Myers, the company's first head of inclusion, stepped down, after working under her for about four years. He is a former NFL player. Before Netflix he advised companies including Google, Procter & Gamble and Viacom on inclusive workplace culture.\n\n### Valarie Toda · full profile →\n\nVice President, Talent\n\nValarie Toda was named VP of Talent at Netflix in October 2019. She leads the HR team that supports the product and technology, legal, global affairs, games and talent organizations. She joined Netflix in 2009 and has led Talent Global Business Practices and served as VP of Talent Acquisition. She began her HR career in recruiting.\n\nFAQ\n\n## Frequently asked questions\n\n### Who leads Netflix?\n\nNetflix is led by Ted Sarandos, its Co-Chief Executive Officer, alongside 29 other tracked leaders such as Greg Peters (Co-CEO) and Spencer Neumann (Chief Financial Officer) (as of August 2026).\n\n### Who is part of Netflix's executive team?\n\nNetflix's tracked executive team includes Ted Sarandos (Co-Chief Executive Officer), Greg Peters (Co-CEO), Spencer Neumann (Chief Financial Officer), Elizabeth Stone (Chief Product and Technology Officer), Marian Lee (Chief Marketing Officer), Bela Bajaria (Chief Content Officer), and others (as of August 2026). See the full list and org chart above.\n\n### How many executives does Netflix have?\n\nNetflix has 30 tracked executives as of August 2026. The company has around 18,677 tracked employee profiles in total.\n\n### What roles are on Netflix's leadership team?\n\nNetflix's leadership roles include Co-Chief Executive Officer, Co-CEO, Chief Financial Officer, Chief Product and Technology Officer, Chief Marketing Officer, Chief Content Officer, Chief Legal Officer, Chief Communications Officer (as of August 2026).\n\n### How can I contact Netflix's executives?\n\nYou can find and verify each leader's professional email and direct phone number with Derrick, from its web app or Google Sheets. Addresses generally follow the flast@netflix.com pattern, but individual addresses are not published here, so confirm before reaching out.\n\nDerrick\n\n## Want emails and phone numbers for Netflix?\n\nAnd for hundreds of companies like it, in one go. Derrick finds the contacts, enriches them and hands them back ready to use.\n\n Create a free account →\n\n100 free credits every month. No credit card.","author":null,"published_date":"2026-09-02","latency_ms":953.331007000088,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}